{# Jinja2 template for runs/<id>/report.md. Order is reviewer-first:
   verdict + workspace + final message at the top; full prompt + tool
   trajectory + DNS log collapsed at the bottom.

   Every emission of opaque content (prompt, file bodies, JSON, dns.log)
   uses <pre>{{ value | e }}</pre>. <pre> blocks are not re-parsed as
   markdown by GFM renderers, so embedded triple-backticks / `#` headings
   / HTML tags inside agent-produced content cannot leak into the report
   layout. The `| e` filter HTML-escapes <, >, &, " so claude's literal
   `</details>` etc. stays inert.

   Avoid embedding markdown inside <details> bodies — keep summaries on
   the outer markdown layer and put everything else under <pre>.
#}
